Repair the following Java 11 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.
Print your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:
<repaired_code>
<your_repaired_code>
</repaired_code>
<confidence>
<your_confidence_score>
</confidence>
Do not provide any other text or markdown fences.

Here is the problem description:
<problem_description>
Mr. Chanek has an integer represented by a string $$$s$$$. Zero or more digits have been erased and are denoted by the character _. There are also zero or more digits marked by the character X, meaning they're the same digit.Mr. Chanek wants to count the number of possible integer $$$s$$$, where $$$s$$$ is divisible by $$$25$$$. Of course, $$$s$$$ must not contain any leading zero. He can replace the character _ with any digit. He can also replace the character X with any digit, but it must be the same for every character X.As a note, a leading zero is any 0 digit that comes before the first nonzero digit in a number string in positional notation. For example, 0025 has two leading zeroes. An exception is the integer zero, (0 has no leading zero, but 0000 has three leading zeroes).
</problem_description>

Here is the Java 11 code you have to repair:
<original_code>
import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;
// Problem Link: https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/1575/D
public class div25 {
    public static char[] str;
    public static int S;
    public static void main (String[] args) throws IOException {
        BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));
        str = in.readLine().toCharArray();
        S = str.length;
        int ans = 0;
        if (S==1) {
            if (str[0]=='X' || str[0] == '_' || Integer.parseInt(String.valueOf(str[0])) == 0) ans = 1;
        }
        else {
            ans += count_possibilities(2, 5);
            ans += count_possibilities(5, 0);
            ans += count_possibilities(7, 5);
            ans += count_possibilities(0, 0); }
        System.out.println(ans);


    }
    static int count_possibilities(int end1, int end2) {
        //System.out.println(end1 + " " + end2);
        int X_val = -1;
        if (str[S-2]=='X') X_val = end1;
        else {
            if (str[S-2]!='_') {
                if (value(S-2) != end1) return 0; } }
        //System.out.println("reached here");
        if (str[S-1]=='X') {
            if (X_val != -1 && end2 != X_val) return 0;
            else X_val = end2; }
        else {
            if (str[S-1]!='_') {
                if (value(S-1) != end2) return 0; } }
        //System.out.println("reached HERE");
        int total = 1;
        for (int i=0;i<S-2;i++) {
//            System.out.println(total);
//            System.out.println(X_val);
//            System.out.println(i + " " + str[i]);
            if (i==0) {
                if (str[i]=='X' && X_val==0) return 0;
                if (value(0) == 0) return 0; }
            if (str[i]=='_') {
                if (i==0) total *= 9;
                else total *= 10; }
            if (str[i]=='X') {
                if (X_val != -1) continue;
                else {
                    X_val = 10; // represents that X can be any integer from 0 to 9 (or possibly 1 to 9)
                    if (i==0) total *= 9;
                    else total *= 10;
                }
            }
        }
        //System.out.println(total);
        return total;
    }

    static boolean isDigit(int pos) {
        if (str[pos]=='_' || str[pos]=='X') return false;
        else return true;
    }

    static int value(int pos) {
        if (!isDigit(pos)) return -1;
        return Integer.parseInt(String.valueOf(str[pos]));
    }
}

